    "updated_at": "2023-01-24T10:24:50Z",
    "body": "Web standard developers have no right to break the web and if you don't want to break it, you'll have to check it - this is a pretty popular pattern - and if it does, you'll have to rename these methods. If not - you will have the same issues as now happening here https://github.com/tc39/proposal-array-grouping/issues/44. The post you mentioned has absolutely nothing to do with this issue since this post has nothing about changing web standards.",
